 "differences": [
  "The deposit's anthropometric table lists one participant as 2015016; no such folder exists and the folder 2014016 (absent from the table) has the same height and weight, so the row is assigned to 2014016.",
  "Age, sex, height, mass and leg lengths are those of the deposit's anthropometric table (a PDF), which reproduces the paper's 24 women, 26 men and age 37.0 +- 13.6 years. The SUBJECT parameters inside the C3D files disagree with that table for 1 participant(s) in gender and 27 in age and were not used.",
  "The paper gives a mean mass of 71.0 kg; the deposit's table gives 71.2 kg, so that number is not used as a check.",
  "66 of the 1193 files (marker count by file: {44: 23, 48: 35, 51: 8, 52: 1127}) hold fewer than 52 markers: the authors left out markers that could not be tracked; each row lists its own markers in channels.",
  "0 of 14690383 marker positions are all zero (0.000%): markers the authors could not reconstruct; kept as shared.",
  "The paper counts 1143 trials as walking trials; the 50 static trials (one per participant) are carried as well, as one-frame marker recordings.",
  "The force and moment channels (Fx1...Mz2) are the C3D's analog channels, expressed in each force plate's coordinate system; the force plate structures that the authors describe (centre of pressure, force and moment in the laboratory frame) are not stored in the C3D files and are not reconstructed here."
